  "limitations": [
    "The SIGINT manager cleanup stopped both active worker PIDs and left both starts pending, but this pre-registered config had max_attempts=1 (one total attempt), so a subsequent resume correctly made no retry and returned partial; the retryable follow-up is EXP-036 with max_attempts=2.",
    "The separate manager-SIGTERM case passed: children continued under inherited OS locks, resume was refused while PIDs/locks remained active, then completed result files were adopted after worker exit without re-running tasks.",
    "Result/task/source/constraint tampering checks were performed only on disposable copies, not on the source run.",
    "Only two starts and five optimizer iterations per 30/35 dB stage were used; no RF performance conclusion is drawn.",
    "Finite-grid checks are screening evidence only; no physical validation was performed.",
    "The task inputs were generated from saved-checkpoint components before canonical terminal remapping was recognized. The lifecycle/recovery assertions remain valid for bounded legal Full-LPF tasks, but these outputs are not checkpoint re-evaluation or candidate-quality evidence."
  ]
